that you have doubts.

164
00:09:12,469 --> 00:09:15,681
Okay, if the situation were
reversed, I'd have doubts too.

165
00:09:15,764 --> 00:09:18,225
And I realize what I'm
suggesting is incredibly risky--

166
00:09:18,308 --> 00:09:20,102
It's fucking suicide.

167
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:21,520
Maybe--
Maybe for some, yeah.

168
00:09:21,603 --> 00:09:23,730
Oh, you're okay with that?

169
00:09:23,814 --> 00:09:25,691
What, we lose a couple
of people?

170
00:09:25,774 --> 00:09:28,277
Maybe a dozen?
How many is too many, Jade?

171
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,945
How many people are gonna
die if you keep

172
00:09:30,028 --> 00:09:31,905
sitting on your goddamn hands
doing nothing?

173
00:09:31,989 --> 00:09:33,407
How many have
you already lost, huh?

174
00:09:33,490 --> 00:09:35,492
What the fuck did
you say to me?

175
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:38,370
Say it again! Go ahead!
Say it again!

176
00:09:38,453 --> 00:09:41,331
Boyd, there is only so long

177
00:09:41,415 --> 00:09:43,208
that you can hold
this place together

178
00:09:43,292 --> 00:09:46,461
with grit
and good intentions.

179
00:09:46,545 --> 00:09:48,005
At some point,
something's gonna give.

180
00:09:48,088 --> 00:09:49,965
Something's gonna change.

181
00:09:50,048 --> 00:09:51,300
You're gonna lose this whole
fucking town.

182
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:04,604
Don't push me, Jade.

183
00:10:04,688 --> 00:10:06,231
This is our chance, Boyd.

184
00:10:07,816 --> 00:10:10,902
I went looking for answers
and I found answers.

185
00:10:10,986 --> 00:10:12,571
This is our shot.

186
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,458
What was that about?

187
00:10:26,001 --> 00:10:28,045
Let's go outside.

188
00:10:35,761 --> 00:10:38,847
So, Jade thinks that digging
up these bones

189
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:42,517
is gonna somehow
help us get home?

190
00:10:42,601 --> 00:10:46,396
If the bones are even down there
in the first place, yeah.

191
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:49,274
That's his theory.

192
00:10:49,358 --> 00:10:52,611
And Jade and Tabitha have
these memories because...

193
00:10:52,694 --> 00:10:54,071
reincarnation.

194
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:55,113
Yeah.

195
00:10:57,074 --> 00:10:58,408
Boyd, what do you think?

196
00:11:00,827 --> 00:11:05,207
If you'd asked me before I got
worms under my skin,

197
00:11:05,290 --> 00:11:08,001
or before I found magic rocks
in the forest

198
00:11:08,085 --> 00:11:11,004
that protect us from monsters,
what the--

199
00:11:11,088 --> 00:11:12,756
Oh, look, I wasn't--

200
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:15,634
I wasn't tryin' to keep any of
this from you.

201
00:11:15,717 --> 00:11:17,177
- I just--
- I know, I know, I know.

202
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:20,722
And I know things haven't
exactly been quiet lately.

203
00:11:20,806 --> 00:11:22,641
They have not.

204
00:11:24,434 --> 00:11:28,105
Remember the good old days when
we used to count the nights

205
00:11:28,188 --> 00:11:30,065
where nothing
bad would happen?

206
00:11:30,148 --> 00:11:31,942
If you'd have told me that was
the good part--

207
00:11:34,486 --> 00:11:36,738
There is something else
we need to talk about.

208
00:11:36,822 --> 00:11:38,073
Look.

209
00:11:44,371 --> 00:11:45,914
Oh my God, what's he doing?

210
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:49,751
Hey. What's goin' on?

211
00:11:49,835 --> 00:11:51,753
- Victor's on the roof.
- What?

212
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:57,634
- Shit.
- What the--

213
00:11:57,717 --> 00:11:59,553
Goddammit.

214
00:12:04,099 --> 00:12:05,475
Victor!

215
00:12:17,529 --> 00:12:19,322
Pretty nice view.

216
00:12:21,741 --> 00:12:23,160
What are you doing up here?

217
00:12:29,541 --> 00:12:32,711
When I was a boy,
a man jumped from here.

218
00:12:34,296 --> 00:12:38,008
He hated this place
so much,

219
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:40,886
and he was so scared all the
time, so one day he jumped.

220
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:45,849
It took days for him
to finally die.

221
00:12:50,479 --> 00:12:55,400
He was trying to fix things
but he just made them worse.

222
00:13:01,615 --> 00:13:04,451
Are you here because
of what I told my dad?

223
00:13:06,411 --> 00:13:07,829
Yeah.

224
00:13:12,083 --> 00:13:15,045
I shouldn't have told him
any of that.

225
00:13:15,128 --> 00:13:16,338
Hey, Victor.

226
00:13:17,881 --> 00:13:20,509
The man in the suit,

227
00:13:20,592 --> 00:13:23,386
he came here
just like everybody else.

228
00:13:26,348 --> 00:13:28,850
Is there anything else you can
remember about him?

229
00:13:31,186 --> 00:13:33,146
Hey, hey, Vi-ctor.

230
00:13:41,029 --> 00:13:42,447
I can try.

231
00:13:43,907 --> 00:13:45,450
Okay.

232
00:13:46,868 --> 00:13:48,370
Why don't we go inside?

233
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:17,857
Sara.

234
00:14:17,941 --> 00:14:19,109
Julie.

235
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:21,486
Hi.

236
00:14:21,570 --> 00:14:24,072
Uh, what's the paint for?

237
00:14:24,155 --> 00:14:27,826
I wanted to do something nice
for Sophia.

238
00:14:27,909 --> 00:14:29,953
Make her feel more
at home.

239
00:14:30,036 --> 00:14:32,122
Nathan always used to say,
"A fresh coat of paint

240
00:14:32,205 --> 00:14:33,415
will fix all your woes."

241
00:14:33,498 --> 00:14:38,378
I-- I don't know what color's
in the cans.

242
00:14:38,461 --> 00:14:42,549
Uh, look, I just wanted
to say I'm sorry.

243
00:14:44,259 --> 00:14:46,845
I didn't really understand
what you went through.

244
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:50,557
But I think I do now.

245
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:53,560
Yeah.
Just wanted to say sorry.

246
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:56,187
Do you wanna help?

247
00:14:58,857 --> 00:15:01,484
I have an extra brush.
Come on inside.

248
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:16,291
This man in yellow...

249
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:18,043
you told your dad
he came to town

250
00:15:18,126 --> 00:15:19,377
just like everybody else.

251
00:15:21,004 --> 00:15:23,548
We thought
his suit was funny.

252
00:15:23,632 --> 00:15:26,801
He seemed like a nice man.

253
00:15:26,885 --> 00:15:28,637
Was he alone
when he came here?

254
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:30,555
Yes. I think so--

