00:29:57,755 --> 00:30:01,258
I promise, I'll explain
everything later.

516
00:30:01,342 --> 00:30:03,010
Jade! I need your help.

517
00:30:03,093 --> 00:30:05,846
Donna needs your help.
Get your shit together.

518
00:30:05,930 --> 00:30:07,598
- Okay! All right.
- Thank you!

519
00:30:07,681 --> 00:30:08,766
Get the wires.

520
00:30:10,518 --> 00:30:11,477
Come on.

521
00:30:13,229 --> 00:30:16,941
Look. Watch out.

522
00:30:17,024 --> 00:30:19,944
What's going on in
there? Is she gonna be okay?

523
00:30:26,909 --> 00:30:29,828
Mom? What happened?

524
00:30:29,912 --> 00:30:31,956
I thought you were outside.

525
00:30:33,999 --> 00:30:35,876
Why is everyone standing by
Donna's room?

526
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:37,044
Um...

527
00:30:40,130 --> 00:30:41,215
Donna had a heart attack.

528
00:30:44,176 --> 00:30:47,263
But she's okay, right?
Is she okay?

529
00:30:47,346 --> 00:30:49,848
We don't know yet.

530
00:30:49,932 --> 00:30:53,102
Everyone's doing whatever
they can. Hey--

531
00:30:53,185 --> 00:30:56,480
But she was fine. Is it
because of the settlement?

532
00:30:56,564 --> 00:30:58,065
- No.
- Because of the dolls?

533
00:30:58,148 --> 00:31:01,026
No, no, no, it's...

534
00:31:01,110 --> 00:31:04,697
honey, sometimes things like
this just happen to people.

535
00:31:04,780 --> 00:31:06,699
- I wanna go see her!
- Ethan--

536
00:31:06,782 --> 00:31:08,450
I wanna see her before
she dies.

537
00:31:08,534 --> 00:31:11,495
Hey. Don't say that.
She's not gonna die.

538
00:31:11,579 --> 00:31:14,456
Yes, she is.
Everyone here dies.

539
00:31:14,540 --> 00:31:16,709
So, please.

540
00:31:16,792 --> 00:31:19,753
Just let me say goodbye.
Please.

541
00:31:31,056 --> 00:31:34,560
Okay. Almost--
Almost got it.

542
00:31:36,979 --> 00:31:38,772
Okay, we got it.

543
00:31:38,856 --> 00:31:40,190
All right. Well?

544
00:31:40,274 --> 00:31:43,027
Well, her vitals
are really stable,

545
00:31:43,110 --> 00:31:45,487
which is-- which is good.

546
00:31:45,571 --> 00:31:48,657
Okay. Then why isn't she awake?

547
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:51,952
Hey, no, talk to me.

548
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:55,247
Well, we just don't know
how long

549
00:31:55,331 --> 00:31:57,041
her brain's been deprived
of oxygen for.

550
00:31:58,917 --> 00:32:00,836
She's gonna wake up.

551
00:32:02,671 --> 00:32:04,506
Kristi?

552
00:32:04,590 --> 00:32:05,883
I don't know.

553
00:32:10,471 --> 00:32:13,223
Hey. Um...

554
00:32:13,307 --> 00:32:16,685
Tabitha's asking if she could
bring Ethan in here

555
00:32:16,769 --> 00:32:17,770
for a second.

556
00:32:17,853 --> 00:32:19,355
He's just really upset.

557
00:32:19,438 --> 00:32:20,939
Uh, yeah, just
for a second though.

558
00:32:21,023 --> 00:32:22,024
Okay.

559
00:32:28,739 --> 00:32:30,157
Donna?

560
00:32:34,328 --> 00:32:36,747
I won't forget what you said.

561
00:32:38,999 --> 00:32:41,126
That fear
is what makes us heroes.

562
00:32:46,173 --> 00:32:48,509
I promise I'll always
do my best to be brave.

563
00:32:56,141 --> 00:32:57,601
I love you, Donna.

564
00:33:14,743 --> 00:33:16,245
That doesn't get any better,
does it?

565
00:33:16,328 --> 00:33:17,871
No.

566
00:33:17,955 --> 00:33:19,998
It does not.

567
00:33:20,082 --> 00:33:24,211
And that, it seems,
is the end of that.

568
00:33:29,299 --> 00:33:32,803
I say we go
for bottle number two.

569
00:33:32,886 --> 00:33:36,557
My dear, I cannot find it
in my heart to disagree.

570
00:33:38,058 --> 00:33:39,309
I can--
I-I can get it.

571
00:33:41,311 --> 00:33:42,771
Ah...

572
00:34:04,793 --> 00:34:06,462
Can I ask you something?

573
00:34:06,545 --> 00:34:08,422
Fire away.

574
00:34:14,470 --> 00:34:18,265
Why were you staring at that
suit in the Sheriff's Station?

575
00:34:23,520 --> 00:34:26,106
I'm sorry. I didn't--
I didn't mean to pry.

576
00:34:26,190 --> 00:34:29,151
No, it's all right,
it's just...

577
00:34:31,737 --> 00:34:34,156
the man who wore that suit.

578
00:34:35,783 --> 00:34:39,369
He did things.
To my family.

579
00:34:40,829 --> 00:34:42,831
He did horrible things.

580
00:34:44,291 --> 00:34:46,502
You have family here?

581
00:34:46,585 --> 00:34:50,339
Well, just my son now.

582
00:34:50,422 --> 00:34:54,051
He came here with my wife
and daughter...

583
00:34:54,134 --> 00:34:56,386
forty years ago.

584
00:34:58,305 --> 00:35:01,767
And that--that man.
Where is he now?

585
00:35:01,850 --> 00:35:03,894
Rotting in hell, I hope.

586
00:35:09,983 --> 00:35:11,485
I say we drink
to your family.

587
00:35:13,028 --> 00:35:14,696
And to your father.

588
00:35:14,780 --> 00:35:16,824
And to my dad.

589
00:35:22,037 --> 00:35:23,831
Wait.

590
00:35:23,914 --> 00:35:26,625
There has to be something
around here

591
00:35:26,708 --> 00:35:28,126
that'll make that
taste better.

592
00:35:28,210 --> 00:35:31,213
Uh, there's not. Trust me.
I've-I've looked.

593
00:35:32,965 --> 00:35:36,844
Well, maybe you just didn't
look hard enou--

594
00:35:36,927 --> 00:35:38,846
Ow!

595
00:35:40,138 --> 00:35:42,057
What happened?

596
00:35:44,017 --> 00:35:46,019
Just some broken glass.

597
00:35:46,103 --> 00:35:49,147
Ooh, uh, well, now.

598
00:35:49,231 --> 00:35:51,233
That doesn't look too bad.
Lemme see.

599
00:35:51,316 --> 00:35:55,404
There's gotta be a clean rag
around here somewhere.

600
00:36:04,079 --> 00:36:06,623
You closed?
What're you doin'?

601
00:36:06,707 --> 00:36:08,917
I'm gonna make food for
everyone up at Colony House.

602
00:36:09,001 --> 00:36:10,586
Why?

603
00:36:10,669 --> 00:36:11,795
Donna.

604
00:36:11,879 --> 00:36:14,256
She had a heart attack.

605
00:36:14,339 --> 00:36:15,924
Oh shit.

606
00:36:16,008 --> 00:36:19,303
Um, is she okay?

607
00:36:19,386 --> 00:36:20,721
We don't know yet.

608
00:36:22,431 --> 00:36:24,641
You want some help?

609
00:36:24,725 --> 00:36:26,226
That'd be nice.

610
00:36:26,310 --> 00:36:27,769
Lemme take that.

611
00:36:33,817 --> 00:36:37,029
It's weird doing
something normal.

612
00:36:37,112 --> 00:36:38,989
I'd almost forgotten
what it was like.

613
00:36:41,283 --> 00:36:43,243
What do you miss most?

614
00:36:43,327 --> 00:36:46,246
Like, not the obvious things--
the little things.

615
00:36:49,625 --> 00:36:53,462
Candy.
I-- I miss candy.

616
00:36:53,545 --> 00:36:56,006
I had a real sweet tooth.

617
00:36:57,841 --> 00:36:59,635
What?

618
00:36:59,718 --> 00:37:01,929
Nothing.

619
00:37:02,012 --> 00:37:03,889
I'm trying to picture you
on a couch somewhere

620
00:37:03,972 --> 00:37:06,224
eating a box of Milk Duds.

621
00:37:06,308 --> 00:37:09,978
Oh. I was more partial
to gummy worms.

622
00:37:10,062 --> 00:37:11,897
Gummy bears.

623
00:37:11,980 --> 00:37:13,357
Really, all things gummy.

624
00:37:13,440 --> 00:37:15,359
I like doughnuts.

625
00:37:15,442 --> 00:37:19,279
Oh, doughnuts.

626
00:37:19,363 --> 00:37:22,866
Yeah, I forgot
about doughnuts.

627
00:37:24,826 --> 00:37:26,203
There was this-- this store

628
00:37:26,286 --> 00:37:28,747
that my dad used to take me--
this doughnut shop--

629
00:37:28,830 --> 00:37:30,999
when I was a little girl.

630
00:37:31,083 --> 00:37:34,378
Just me and him.

631
00:37:34,461 --> 00:37:37,339
A stupid
daddy/daughter thing.

632
00:37:39,883 --> 00:37:42,803
But one day I...

633
00:37:42,886 --> 00:37:45,681
I told him I didn't
want to go anymore.

634
00:37:45,764 --> 00:37:47,307
I just wanted to hang out
with my friends.

635
00:37:50,686 --> 00:37:52,479
I wish that I...

636
00:38:06,660 --> 00:38:09,454
Can I
ask you something?

637
00:38:11,206 --> 00:38:12,374
Sure.

638
00:38:14,543 --> 00:38:16,378
Before, you said

639
00:38:16,461 --> 00:38:18,588
you understood
what I went through.

640
00:38:21,133 --> 00:38:22,092
How?

641
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:27,973
Something here convinced me

642
00:38:28,056 --> 00:38:31,226
that I could
still help my dad.

643
00:38:33,854 --> 00:38:38,608
Like, I could go back
to the day it happened and...

644
00:38:38,692 --> 00:38:40,193
I could--
I could save him.

645
00:38:45,741 --> 00:38:49,619
I can't do that.
Can I?

646
00:39:07,387 --> 00:39:10,098
I'm so sorry
that happened to you.

647
00:39:28,867 --> 00:39:30,077
Hey.

648
00:39:31,828 --> 00:39:32,746
Any news?

649
00:39:32,829 --> 00:39:35,874
No. No, nothing.
Nothing yet.

650
00:39:35,957 --> 00:39:38,376
You, uh, you talk
to Fatima?

651
00:39:38,460 --> 00:39:39,878
Yeah.

652
00:39:39,961 --> 00:39:41,046
And?

653
00:39:43,548 --> 00:39:46,468
Well, my wife is building a
monster in a room full of dirt.

654
00:39:46,551 --> 00:39:48,136
Hmm.

655
00:39:48,220 --> 00:39:51,890
And, yet, I think it's exactly
what she needs right now.

656
00:39:51,973 --> 00:39:53,642
Yeah.

657
00:39:59,064 --> 00:40:00,899
She awake?

658
00:40:00,982 --> 00:40:02,067
No, not yet.

659
00:40:07,364 --> 00:40:08,949
You can go sit with
her if you want.

660
00:40:19,876 --> 00:40:20,836
Hey.

661
00:40:20,919 --> 00:40:21,837
Hey.

662
00:40:24,256 --> 00:40:26,967
I'll give you some space.

663
00:40:27,050 --> 00:40:28,468
All right.

664
00:40:30,470 --> 00:40:32,347
If anything changes,
you let me know.

665
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:33,807
Yeah.

666
00:40:33,890 --> 00:40:37,310
- I'll just be outside.
- Okay.

667
00:40:48,280 --> 00:40:51,116
All right, you can cut the shit
now and open your eyes.

668
00:40:58,874 --> 00:41:03,461
I want you to listen to me.

669
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:06,339
Okay?

670
00:41:08,216 --> 00:41:09,968
I cannot...

671
00:41:14,973 --> 00:41:18,602
I cannot do this
without you.

672
00:41:20,187 --> 00:41:25,025
So you better wake the hell up,
you hear me?

673
00:41:25,108 --> 00:41:27,611
We got things to do,
you and me.

674
00:41:29,654 --> 00:41:33,158
I'm not saying goodbye,
you understand?

675
00:41:35,285 --> 00:41:37,787
I ain't fucking
saying goodbye.

676
00:41:40,916 --> 00:41:43,460
What are you
gonna do if she doesn't wake up?

677
00:41:45,086 --> 00:41:47,464
What the hell
kinda question is that?

678
00:41:47,547 --> 00:41:49,299
A practical one.

679
00:41:53,136 --> 00:41:55,680
Make sure you get
those nice and thin.

680
00:41:55,764 --> 00:41:57,390
I said I'd help,

681
00:41:57,474 --> 00:41:59,434
not cut off my fingers
for a pot of your stew.

682
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:00,936
It's really good stew.

683
00:42:01,019 --> 00:42:01,978
Mm-hm.

684
00:42:04,856 --> 00:42:07,025
Uh, make them
a little bit chunkier.

685
00:42:08,693 --> 00:42:10,070
Why are you lurking
over there in the corner?

686
00:42:10,153 --> 00:42:11,655
Get in here and chop some
veggies.

687
00:42:11,738 --> 00:42:14,032
- Oh, no, I was--
- I wasn't askin'.

688
00:42:15,659 --> 00:42:16,701
Okay.

689
00:42:30,006 --> 00:42:32,008
We're a handsome
fuckin' pair, huh?

690
00:42:37,472 --> 00:42:39,266
You remember the night

691
00:42:39,349 --> 00:42:44,187
that me, Abby,
and Ellis rolled into town?

692
00:42:44,271 --> 00:42:48,608
Yeah. Pretty sure Abby
wanted you to shoot me.

693
00:42:48,692 --> 00:42:51,278
You scared
the shit out of us!

694
00:42:51,361 --> 00:42:53,029
Runnin' into the middle
of the street

695
00:42:53,113 --> 00:42:55,115
like a goddamn lunatic!

696
00:42:55,198 --> 00:42:59,452
Then you bring us down
into some dugout bunker--

697
00:42:59,536 --> 00:43:02,956
and there was Donna.

698
00:43:03,039 --> 00:43:05,542
And Dale-- Dale, Dale was
there too. You know.

699
00:43:07,127 --> 00:43:09,587
Remember the first question
Donna asked me?

700
00:43:11,256 --> 00:43:13,049
No.

701
00:43:13,133 --> 00:43:15,093
"Do any of you snore?"

702
00:43:18,763 --> 00:43:21,516
I didn't know what the fuck
she was talking about.

703
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:25,478
We just heard monsters
screeching in the forest

704
00:43:25,562 --> 00:43:26,938
and then climbed
into a hole,

705
00:43:27,022 --> 00:43:29,024
and this lady is talking
about snoring.

706
00:43:30,942 --> 00:43:33,278
Then she looked at me,
calm and steady, and said,

707
00:43:34,821 --> 00:43:36,906
"If you snore,
they'll find us."

708
00:43:38,783 --> 00:43:41,202
Right there in the middle
of all the fear,

709
00:43:41,286 --> 00:43:44,789
the disbelief,
the pants-shitting chaos,

710
00:43:46,416 --> 00:43:49,502
little voice in the back
of my head said, "This one--

711
00:43:51,671 --> 00:43:53,673
yeah, she knows
how to survive.

712
00:43:55,675 --> 00:43:57,385
We might be okay."

713
00:43:59,763 --> 00:44:01,348
That's what got me through
that night.

714
00:44:03,433 --> 00:44:05,310
The darkest,
scariest night of my life,

715
00:44:05,393 --> 00:44:06,728
and she's the one that got me
through it.

716
00:44:09,105 --> 00:44:10,982
I don't think
I ever told her that.

717
00:44:13,068 --> 00:44:16,571
We, did we bump heads in
the beginning.

718
00:44:16,654 --> 00:44:21,659
She made it very clear that
she did not like me at all.

719
00:44:21,743 --> 00:44:22,786
No sir.

720
00:44:24,204 --> 00:44:27,040
So, what changed?

721
00:44:27,123 --> 00:44:29,376
I don't know,
I like to think that

722
00:44:30,919 --> 00:44:32,962
we got to know each other
a little.

723
00:44:38,343 --> 00:44:41,930
The answer is, I don't have
the slightest fucking idea.

724
00:44:42,013 --> 00:44:43,348
Answer to what?

725
00:44:43,431 --> 00:44:44,766
You asked me what
I was gonna do

726
00:44:44,849 --> 00:44:46,684
if she didn't wake up.

727
00:44:46,768 --> 00:44:48,520
Then it's time to get these
people home.

728
00:44:50,230 --> 00:44:52,065
Look, this might not be
the moment to bring this up,

729
00:44:52,148 --> 00:44:55,402
but Jade already told you
what you need to do.

730
00:44:55,485 --> 00:44:59,072
You're really just gonna ignore
that over a missing door?

731
00:44:59,155 --> 00:45:01,241
I mean, the fact that Donna's
lying here right now--

732
00:45:01,324 --> 00:45:03,993
You're right. This is not
the goddamn moment!

733
00:45:08,498 --> 00:45:09,874
Boyd?

734
00:45:14,754 --> 00:45:17,465
Oh, hey, hey, hey, hey.
Oh, shh, shh, shh.

735
00:45:17,549 --> 00:45:18,842
It's okay.

736
00:45:18,925 --> 00:45:21,553
No, no, no, no.
You're okay.

737
00:45:21,636 --> 00:45:23,596
- Boyd?
- Hey, do-- hey. You're here.

738
00:45:23,680 --> 00:45:25,890
You're okay-- Kristi!

739
00:45:25,974 --> 00:45:27,725
You're here. You're here.

740
00:45:27,809 --> 00:45:29,477
- What?
- Get in here, get in, get in.

741
00:45:29,561 --> 00:45:32,647
You're okay.
You're okay.

742
00:45:32,730 --> 00:45:33,982
- Hey.
- You're all right.

743
00:45:34,065 --> 00:45:36,151
Donna?
Hey, Donna.

744
00:45:36,234 --> 00:45:37,360
Oh, God.

745
00:45:37,444 --> 00:45:38,820
I know.
Can you look at me? Donna?

746
00:45:38,903 --> 00:45:40,738
- Hey, hey.
- Just breathe.

747
00:45:40,822 --> 00:45:42,240
Good.

748
00:45:42,323 --> 00:45:46,911
Yeah.

749
00:45:46,995 --> 00:45:49,706
You need to squeeze
my hands, okay?

750
00:45:51,249 --> 00:45:52,709
Okay.

751
00:45:56,087 --> 00:45:57,547
- Uh, Dad?
- Uh, yeah.

752
00:45:57,630 --> 00:45:58,965
Uh, she's awake.

753
00:45:59,048 --> 00:46:00,884
Oh my God.

754
00:46:00,967 --> 00:46:03,261
She's uh--
hey, would you, uh--

755
00:46:03,344 --> 00:46:05,180
- Okay.
- Would you tell everybody?

756
00:46:05,263 --> 00:46:06,556
Thank you.

757
00:46:07,765 --> 00:46:08,600
Yeah.

758
00:46:10,018 --> 00:46:11,394
Hey, guys, she's awake!

759
00:46:11,478 --> 00:46:12,854
Yeah.
Hey, did you hear that?

760
00:46:12,937 --> 00:46:14,105
Yeah.

761
00:46:14,189 --> 00:46:15,607
Guys, she's awake!

762
00:46:15,690 --> 00:46:18,318
Hey. She's okay?

763
00:46:18,401 --> 00:46:20,403
Yeah. Yeah, she is.

764
00:46:20,487 --> 00:46:22,655
- Okay.
- She's, uh-- yeah.

765
00:46:22,739 --> 00:46:23,823
Okay.

766
00:46:23,907 --> 00:46:25,700
I'll be--
I'll be right back.

767
00:46:27,744 --> 00:46:30,705
Uh, there you go.
Good as new.

768
00:46:30,788 --> 00:46:32,123
Sort of.

769
00:46:32,207 --> 00:46:34,542
Should we drink
to my good health?

770
00:46:34,626 --> 00:46:36,044
Why not?

771
00:46:43,676 --> 00:46:46,804
Ooh.
That one had some kick.

772
00:46:48,932 --> 00:46:50,767
You know what I was
thinking, Henry?

773
00:46:50,850 --> 00:46:52,602
I do not.

774
00:46:52,685 --> 00:46:56,314
But I am near certain you
are about to tell me.

775
00:46:56,397 --> 00:47:00,068
It's the strangest thought,
but I just can't shake it.

776
00:47:00,151 --> 00:47:04,447
You know, we're trapped in a
town we can't escape from,

777
00:47:04,531 --> 00:47:07,742
